          wrongTurn: 'The wrong turn is answering questions as they arrive, because being helpful is the natural thing to do and it destroys the result. The questions are the finding, and answering them in the room deletes the evidence.',
          tradeoff: 'Refusing to answer for twenty minutes feels obstructive, and the person reading it works more slowly than they would have with you narrating.',
          uncertainty: 'Still unknown: how many holes remain that this reader happened not to hit. One reader finds the holes one reader finds.',
